Text:
This design is about which presses of keys and of mouse buttons a Fearless program can receive.
A Key models one physical key of a keyboard, or one button of a mouse.
A Key is named after its position on the keyboard, with the name that the US layout gives to that position: the Key Q is the first letter key of the top letter row on every keyboard layout.
The left and the right key of a modifier are one Key: the Key Shift is down while at least one of the two shift keys is down.
The Key Super is the key that Windows calls Win and macOS calls Command; the Key Alt is the key that macOS calls Option.
Some keys of a keyboard are of no form Key: the lock keys (CapsLock, NumLock, ScrollLock), PrtSc, Pause, Menu, the keys from F13, and every key that the 105 key PC keyboard does not have, such as the volume keys, the fn key of a laptop and the Globe key.
No Fearless program receives those keys, on any desk.
A Press models one Key going down: Mods says which Modifiers are down at that moment.
A 'desk' is an operating system with its desktop environment, as a user installs it.
Press.unreachable holds for the Presses that at least one desk takes for itself: on that desk no program can receive that Press, or no program can stop what the desk does with that Press.
No Fearless program receives an unreachable Press, on any desk: fearlessManager binds no value to an unreachable Press, and the Fearless GUI does nothing for an unreachable Press, also on a desk where that Press reaches the program.
The desk does with an unreachable Press what the desk does for every program: for example Alt+Tab shows the window switcher of the desk.
Press.reserved holds for the Presses that the Fearless GUI uses for itself, with the same behaviour on every desk.
Every Press with Press.bindable reaches the Fearless GUI on every desk.
//later: the buttons of a mouse after the third, and the buttons of a joypad
//later: inputs that give an amount and not a Press: the movement of the mouse, the wheel, the sticks of a joypad

Grammar:
Modifier ::= "Shift" | "Ctrl" | "Alt" | "Super"
FKey ::= "F" [1-9] | "F1" [0-2]
NamedKey ::= "Esc" | "Tab" | "Space" | "Enter" | "Backspace" | "Ins" | "Del" | "Home" | "End" | "PgUp" | "PgDn"    \
           | "Left" | "Right" | "Up" | "Down"                                                                    \
           | "Backquote" | "Minus" | "Equals" | "LeftBracket" | "RightBracket" | "Backslash"                     \
           | "Semicolon" | "Quote" | "Comma" | "Period" | "Slash" | "IntlBackslash"                              \
           | "NumDivide" | "NumMultiply" | "NumMinus" | "NumPlus" | "NumEnter" | "NumPeriod"
KeyboardKey ::= Modifier | [A-Z] | [0-9] | FKey | NamedKey | "Num" [0-9]
MouseButton ::= "MouseLeft" | "MouseMiddle" | "MouseRight"
Key ::= KeyboardKey | MouseButton
ShiftMod ::= "" | "Shift+"
CtrlMod ::= "" | "Ctrl+"
AltMod ::= "" | "Alt+"
SuperMod ::= "" | "Super+"
Mods ::= ShiftMod CtrlMod AltMod SuperMod
Press ::= Mods Key

Well formedness:
in Press: if Press is Mods Modifier, then Mods does not hold Modifier "+"

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = _ "Super+" Key

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = Mods "Super"

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = "Alt+" Key
- Key is one of Tab, Esc, Backquote, Space, Enter, D, Del, Ins, F1, F2, F3, F5, F6, F7, F8, F9, F10, F11, F12

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = "Shift+Alt+" Key
- Key is one of Tab, Esc, Backquote, Q, F6, Left, Right, Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = "Ctrl+Alt+" Key
- Key is of form FKey, or of form "Num" [1-9], or is one of T, D, L, S, B, I, E, F, Del, Backspace, Esc, Tab, Home, End, Left, Right, Up, Down

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = "Shift+Ctrl+Alt+" Key
- Key is one of Tab, Esc, R, Left, Right, Up, Down

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = "Ctrl+" Key
- Key is of form FKey, or is one of Esc, Left, Right, Up, Down

Notation: Press.unreachable where:
- Press = "Shift+Ctrl+" Key
- Key is one of Esc, F6, F7

Notation: Press.reserved where:
- Press = Mods "Esc"

Notation: Press.reserved where:
- Press = Mods "Tab"

Notation: Press.reserved where:
- Press = "Alt+F4"

Notation: Press.bindable where:
- not Press.unreachable
- not Press.reserved

Implementation notes:
The Notations of Press.unreachable come from measurements on 15 desks: Windows 11, macOS, and the 13 Linux desks ubuntu_gnome, fedora_gnome, debian_gnome_x11, kubuntu_plasma, opensuse_plasma, fedora_cosmic, debian_cinnamon, debian_mate, xubuntu_xfce, lubuntu_lxqt, arch_sway, omarchy_hyprland and void_i3.
Each desk is measured as installed: one keyboard layout, no input method, no shortcut added by the user.
A desk where the user adds a shortcut, or a second keyboard layout, takes more Presses; nothing in this design prevents that, and on that machine such a Press behaves as an unreachable Press that the Fearless GUI does not know.
void_i3 is counted with Super as the modifier of i3: i3 asks at its first start whether its modifier is Win or Alt, and the answer Alt is a setting of the user.
The Fearless GUI takes no key away from the desk: no keyboard grab on X11, no shortcut inhibitor on Wayland, no presentation option on macOS, no low level keyboard hook on Windows.
On GNOME on Wayland, on sway and on Hyprland no such mechanism works for a window of the JVM, which is an X11 window under XWayland; this is why the same rule holds on every desk.
The desks behind each Notation of Press.unreachable:
- Super: every desk; Win on Windows, Command on macOS, the modifier of the desk shortcuts on GNOME, KDE Plasma, COSMIC, sway, Hyprland and i3.
- "Alt+": Tab, Esc on Windows and GNOME; Backquote, Space, F2, F5, F6, F7, F8, F10 on GNOME; Enter, D on sway; F1, F3 on KDE Plasma; F9 on MATE and Xfce; F11, F12, Del, Ins on Xfce.
- "Shift+Alt+": Tab on Windows and GNOME; Esc, Backquote, F6 on GNOME; Q on sway; the arrows on LXQt; PgUp, PgDn on Xfce.
- "Ctrl+Alt+": F1 to F12 switch to a text console on every Linux desk, under every mechanism; Del on Windows; T, D, Esc, Tab, Backspace, the arrows on GNOME; L on LXQt; S on MATE; B, I, E on LXQt; F, Home, End, Num1 to Num9 on Xfce.
- "Shift+Ctrl+Alt+": Esc is taken by systemd-logind on every Linux desk with systemd 258 or later; Tab, R, the arrows on GNOME.
- "Ctrl+": Esc on Windows; the arrows and F1 to F8 on macOS; F1 to F12 on KDE Plasma and Xfce.
- "Shift+Ctrl+": Esc on Windows; F6, F7 on LXQt.
Not measured: Ctrl+Left, Ctrl+Right and Ctrl+Space on macOS, and Ctrl+F2 to Ctrl+F7 on macOS, which act only while the keyboard navigation of macOS is on.
On macOS a laptop gives F1 to F12 only together with the fn key; the Key is the same FKey.
A key that is of no form Key either gives no press and release that a program can pair on some desk (CapsLock on macOS), or is taken by a desk under every Mods (PrtSc, the volume keys, Pause on macOS), or was not measured (Menu).
"Alt+F4" is reserved and not unreachable: Windows, GNOME, KDE Plasma, COSMIC, Cinnamon, MATE, Xfce and LXQt close the window for it, and the Fearless GUI closes the window by itself on the other desks, so the behaviour is the same on every desk.
